WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.382 --> 00:00:01.423
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:01.423 --> 00:00:02.256
- I mean--

00:00:02.256 --> 00:00:03.089
(Arsema chuckles)

00:00:03.089 --> 00:00:05.700
I don't have long enough with you

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.890
and I'm sad about it but I'm,

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:10.500
so we're all fans of
"Bridgerton" in general.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.200
Just, before even this show existed.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.580
But I have to tell you, like
this series, like gets better.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.740
Like you, I watched the
first series like no way,

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:20.970
they're gonna do it with the second one.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:23.280
I was like, oh my god, no way.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.510
They're gonna do the third one.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:25.932
This is my favorite one.

00:00:25.932 --> 00:00:27.140
- No way.
- Wow.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:31.170
- It is, so no, way, way, way it is so good.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:33.270
So tell us, or I know who you play

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:34.440
but tell everybody who you play

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.510
and like what it's really
about your character.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.390
- So I play a young Queen Charlotte.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:42.350
Queen Charlotte is obviously
the queen in "Bridgerton."

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:43.500
So I play the younger version

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.737
of Golda Rosheuvel's portrayal of her.

00:00:46.737 --> 00:00:47.699
- [Corey] She is.

00:00:47.699 --> 00:00:48.779
- [Arsema] There she is.
- Oh my God.

00:00:48.779 --> 00:00:51.249
(audience cheers)

00:00:51.249 --> 00:00:53.226
Looking phenomenal.

00:00:53.226 --> 00:00:54.450
- She's pretty cool.

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:55.283
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:55.283 --> 00:00:56.714
- And that's her.

00:00:56.714 --> 00:00:59.040
She's pretty, yeah, she's 17.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.960
She's come from Germany.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.700
- Kind of a progressive mind for the time.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:03.750
- [India] Yeah, completely.
- Yeah.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:05.250
- And very kind of inquisitive

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.960
and really lovely to play someone

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.060
who's not just one-dimensional

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:11.650
and she's got so many
different layers and yeah,

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:14.130
very lucky to be a part
of it and to play her.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:15.090
- And it's intense.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.713
Y'all, yeah, I was like, what?

00:01:16.713 --> 00:01:18.390
Yeah, okay, tell everybody who is here,

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:19.260
Lady Danbury.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:22.290
- Yes, yeah, I'm young
Lady Agatha Danbury.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:26.370
In the show, you kind of see
her in a much different version

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.443
than you saw in, (Arsema chuckles) yes.

00:01:28.443 --> 00:01:30.990
(audience cheers)

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.280
So like in "Bridgerton,"

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.400
she's this extremely powerful woman.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.423
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:36.423 --> 00:01:37.620
- You know, you see her
with her cane and her hat.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:42.510
And then to see her in this
show, she is just not there yet.

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:44.370
And you kind of see her become that.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.680
So to see what a journey is like

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.754
in a young Black woman is
so just exciting to play.

00:01:48.754 --> 00:01:50.970
- And the pressure and the weight.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.501
I love how this story,

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:56.534
it has a lot of parallels
for just like life now too.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:57.630
You know?

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:58.950
And there's a lot of messaging in there.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:00.150
Not in a way that beats you over the head,

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:03.030
but tells a story to where you
make, it's thought provoking.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:04.042
- Yeah.

00:02:04.042 --> 00:02:05.101
- I just love how you see her

00:02:05.101 --> 00:02:06.420
in a completely different light, you know?

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:07.710
And you did a great job.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:08.910
It was really, really great.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:10.002
- Thank you.

00:02:10.002 --> 00:02:11.973
(audience applauds)

00:02:11.973 --> 00:02:12.979
Thanks.

00:02:12.979 --> 00:02:15.060
- Corey, you can tell
everybody who you play.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:15.893
But oh my gosh,

00:02:15.893 --> 00:02:17.904
I feel like you out of
the entire cast just,

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:20.635
they put you through the
ringer emotionally, like.

00:02:20.635 --> 00:02:22.260
- Yeah, it wasn't easy.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.093
- [Kelly] No.

00:02:23.093 --> 00:02:25.353
- Yeah, these guys made
it very easy, easier.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:27.857
Yeah, not so much India.

00:02:27.857 --> 00:02:29.056
(all laugh)

00:02:29.056 --> 00:02:32.910
No, it was great, yeah, he is charming.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:34.950
He has that string to his bow,

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:37.410
but he, the man that he, there he is.

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:38.243
- Yeah, King George.

00:02:38.243 --> 00:02:39.076
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.393
- Sorry, that--

00:02:41.393 --> 00:02:42.960
- And you play King George, yeah.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:43.920
- Yes.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.060
- Just looking fantastic.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:46.576
Here's the thing.

00:02:46.576 --> 00:02:47.940
I know y'all all look beautiful
and gorgeous and whatever.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:49.290
How uncomfortable were you?

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:51.550
Don't lie.

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:53.760
- Give me a little Arsema,
like, where do we go?

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:54.593
Where do we stop?

00:02:54.593 --> 00:02:56.248
- There's so many choices.

00:02:56.248 --> 00:02:58.320
The shoes, the skirts
themselves were heavy.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:02:59.354
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:59.354 --> 00:03:00.187
- Yeah.

00:03:00.187 --> 00:03:01.020
- The corsets and then the wigs.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:02.236
- Yeah.

00:03:02.236 --> 00:03:03.330
- Which were like another good ten pounds.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:04.800
- I mean, they did a great job.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:05.850
You look incredible.

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:06.683
But I was like,

00:03:06.683 --> 00:03:08.307
there is no way they're
not crying deep inside.

00:03:08.307 --> 00:03:09.140
(Arsema laughs)

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:11.880
- Yeah, it really helps it, I
think I speak for all of us.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:13.620
It helps get into character.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:15.030
It creates authentic character.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:16.170
'Cause you're not having to think,

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:18.120
how would they feel in this corset.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:19.013
You are feeling it.
- 'Cause really wanna die.

00:03:19.013 --> 00:03:20.160
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:20.993
- Exactly, yeah.

00:03:20.993 --> 00:03:22.314
So it doesn't just look fantastic.

00:03:22.314 --> 00:03:24.842
It helps in every way.

00:03:24.842 --> 00:03:26.431
(audience cheers)

00:03:26.431 --> 00:03:27.345
- Where were you originally from?

00:03:27.345 --> 00:03:28.178
You, I feel like you've lived all over.

00:03:28.178 --> 00:03:30.450
- Yeah, so I was born in Atlanta, Georgia.

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:31.530
- Okay.

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:33.167
- And then, yes.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:34.720
- That one.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:35.967
- That is my--
- One person.

00:03:35.967 --> 00:03:36.800
- That's your mom.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:37.633
- It's my mom.

00:03:37.633 --> 00:03:39.341
- It's your mom, oh my God, what's up mom?

00:03:39.341 --> 00:03:41.754
(audience cheers)

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.910
Arsema's mom is in the
audience, all right.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.140
- So she's going to like
double check everything

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:47.070
that I say right now.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:48.090
- Yeah.

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:49.320
- So it's 100% true.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.810
But yeah, then I, we, I moved to New York

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:55.380
and then grew up a lot in,
around Sub-Saharan Africa.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:59.424
So Kenya, Benin, Togo, Uganda,

00:03:59.424 --> 00:04:01.363
and then came back to the States.

00:04:01.363 --> 00:04:03.367
- That can be hard as a kid traveling,

00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:05.953
but what a cool experience to be able to,

00:04:05.953 --> 00:04:08.400
like, what's your favorite
place, if you had to pick.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.080
- Benin is probably my favorite.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.115
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:11.115 --> 00:04:13.680
- It's like this small beautiful
country in West Africa,

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:17.280
Francophone and it's like the
beach is the entire country.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:18.283
You can--

00:04:18.283 --> 00:04:19.400
- That's beautiful.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.233
You're constantly on vacation.

00:04:20.233 --> 00:04:21.345
- Exactly.

00:04:21.345 --> 00:04:22.559
- [Kelly] Even when you're not.

00:04:22.559 --> 00:04:23.667
- Exactly.

00:04:23.667 --> 00:04:24.790
- That's how we should live.

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:25.623
Is it true though that
you and some castmates,

00:04:25.623 --> 00:04:26.460
did y'all rent a Vrbo?

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:28.221
Like after y'all taped?

00:04:28.221 --> 00:04:29.054
- Yeah.

00:04:29.054 --> 00:04:30.240
- We did, no, we, during the taping.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.701
- [Kelly] During it.

00:04:31.701 --> 00:04:32.718
- [Corey] Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:04:32.718 --> 00:04:35.077
So we had like two weeks left
on the job and we thought,

00:04:35.077 --> 00:04:36.210
"Why not spend it all together?"

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.653
We got along like a house
on fire most of the time.

00:04:38.653 --> 00:04:39.486
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:39.486 --> 00:04:42.978
- But yeah, we had a really
good time and we haunted.

00:04:42.978 --> 00:04:46.080
I almost told the whole secret--

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:47.490
- No, that's what I wanna get to--

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:48.510
- Of the story.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:50.990
- Here's the thing, I heard
that the place that you stayed

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:51.823
was haunted.
- [India] Was haunted, yeah.

00:04:51.823 --> 00:04:53.034
- Okay.

00:04:53.034 --> 00:04:54.480
- Well it wasn't, but we thought it was.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.730
- Why did you think it
was, what's that story?

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.135
- His name is Freddy Dennis.

00:04:58.135 --> 00:04:59.992
- [India] And he's in the show.

00:04:59.992 --> 00:05:00.826
- And he's not here with us today.

00:05:00.826 --> 00:05:01.659
- Yes, he is in the show.

00:05:01.659 --> 00:05:04.920
- Yeah, no, he's a trickster.

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:06.350
- [Kelly] Oh, he's a prankster.

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:07.500
- And a fool and a fiend.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:08.333
- [India] But we love him.

00:05:08.333 --> 00:05:09.270
- We love him, yeah, he's amazing.

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:10.560
I live with Freddy now,

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:11.393
but, yeah, he's--
- Wait, does,

00:05:11.393 --> 00:05:12.574
so he's the guy that jumps
out and scares you a lot?

00:05:12.574 --> 00:05:13.590
- Yeah.

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:14.934
- That's not my kind of dude.

00:05:14.934 --> 00:05:15.767
- [India] No.
- [Corey] No.

00:05:15.767 --> 00:05:16.600
(Arsema laughs)

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:17.433
- [Kelly] Not my kind of dude.

00:05:17.433 --> 00:05:18.690
- He turned the lights off
when she was in the shower.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:19.650
- In the shower.

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:20.483
Really dangerous.

00:05:20.483 --> 00:05:21.316
I'm not funny.
- What if you'd been shaving?

00:05:21.316 --> 00:05:22.149
- Exactly.

00:05:22.149 --> 00:05:22.982
- Imagine.

00:05:22.982 --> 00:05:23.880
- Yes, exactly.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.050
Yeah, but we had a really good time.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:25.883
- Oh my God.

00:05:25.883 --> 00:05:26.850
So he didn't, you didn't
know he was doing it though

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:28.237
and they kept saying
the place was haunted.

00:05:28.237 --> 00:05:29.070
- Yeah, exactly.

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:29.903
- Yeah.

00:05:29.903 --> 00:05:32.129
- And you're just like
naked in the shower.

00:05:32.129 --> 00:05:32.962
Like what?

00:05:32.962 --> 00:05:33.910
- Yeah, and I ran down in my towel.

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.531
I was like, "Guys, this
isn't funny anymore.

00:05:35.531 --> 00:05:36.778
"Now it's serious."

00:05:36.778 --> 00:05:38.352
But it was a joke.

00:05:38.352 --> 00:05:39.706
But we had a great time.
- [Kelly] Oh, God.

00:05:39.706 --> 00:05:40.539
- Yeah, it was a great time.

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:41.710
- That's so fun that you
had such great chemistry

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:42.787
that you ended up, you're like,

00:05:42.787 --> 00:05:44.670
"Let's just do this for
the last couple weeks."

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:45.510
That's awesome.

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:46.830
- Yeah (indistinct).
- What a fun, yeah,

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:48.899
it is rare though, it's so good.

00:05:48.899 --> 00:05:52.650
Arsema, so I heard that you
got to meet one of your idols.

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:54.090
Is this right, at the
(indistinct), this year?

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:55.100
- Yeah.
- Serena William?

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:56.346
- At the, I mean, I
didn't get to meet her.

00:05:56.346 --> 00:05:58.767
I must just say that, as a disclaimer.

00:05:58.767 --> 00:06:00.000
- [Kelly] You got to--

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.523
- We made eye contact.

00:06:01.523 --> 00:06:03.713
(audience applauds)

00:06:03.713 --> 00:06:07.320
And then in the most cosmic of timing,

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:10.650
my heel just like broke

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:13.230
and I fell to the floor as if I was,

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:15.480
yep, that's the shoe.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:17.043
- [Kelly] It happens to the best of us.

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:19.410
- Yes, and it looked
just like I had fainted

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:22.860
as though I had just seen
Serena Williams, which she was--

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:24.510
- [Kelly] Was it like
right in front of her?

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.790
- It was like, we were across the room.

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:30.791
She's tall and because of
the platform, so was I.

00:06:30.791 --> 00:06:33.660
And I remember her looking at me

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:36.180
and me looking at her, and
I'm like, are we gonna?

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:39.360
And then I just was like, and
then everyone's like, whoa.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:41.949
And I'm like, okay, I dropped something--

00:06:41.949 --> 00:06:43.080
- Then Satan takes hold of the moment.

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:43.913
- Yeah.

00:06:43.913 --> 00:06:44.943
- The devil was alive on that day.

00:06:44.943 --> 00:06:46.693
- The devil came through.

00:06:46.693 --> 00:06:49.320
Thank y'all so much.

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:51.780
I love, I know that y'all
are off to do something

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:53.760
and I love that you took
the time to do the show

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:56.040
because I really appreciated everything.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:57.540
Just as like someone who loves

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:59.310
a bit of escapism in their life

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:02.160
and to make something just,
it's just so well done.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.140
The acting, the art
direction, the storytelling.

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:07.200
It's so well done.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:09.267
So thank you for doing that for all of us.

00:07:09.267 --> 00:07:10.508
(audience applauds)

00:07:10.508 --> 00:07:11.495
It's so entertaining.

00:07:11.495 --> 00:07:14.910
Everybody, you have got to
watch "Queen Charlotte."

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:15.913
It's the best one out of the "Bridgerton,"

00:07:15.913 --> 00:07:17.494
It's a "Bridgerton" story.

00:07:17.494 --> 00:07:18.327
It's on Netflix.

00:07:18.327 --> 00:07:19.977
It's a great part of this series.

